// Lesson 7.1 — Tilemaps: The Level Editor
//
// SCAFFOLDING: OUTLINE ONLY (level 3), and asks.ts is being changed from 2 to 3
// to match. This is the honest rung because there is NO SCRIPT IN THIS LESSON.
// Tilemaps are editor work from end to end: create or load a palette, select a
// tilemap, paint, erase. The walkthrough primitive gives a student a file to
// type line by line, so a walkthrough here would have to invent a script that
// the lesson does not have — fabricated scaffolding, which is worse than none.
// verify-site refuses a level-3 lesson that renders one, and there is none.
// The Build Lab keeps its procedural steps because 6.4 (also level 3) keeps
// its editor steps — the level-3 bargain withholds the CODE, and there is no
// code here to withhold.
//
// GROUND TRUTH (read out of AP_CS_P_Starter_Project, Unity 6000.6.0f1, by
// parsing Assets/_Scenes/Platformer.unity and the asset folders directly):
//
//   Platformer ▸ Grid — m_CellSize: {x: 1, y: 1, z: 0}. It has THREE tilemap
//     children, all with m_Father pointing at the Grid's Transform:
//       `Collision`    75 tiles, bounding box x -8..7 (16 wide) and y -5..4
//                      (10 tall) — a cave shape, NOT a filled rectangle and
//                      NOT "20 wide and 12 tall", which the old page claimed.
//                      Tag `Ground`, layer 0. TilemapCollider2D
//                      (m_CompositeOperation: 1 = Merge), CompositeCollider2D,
//                      Rigidbody2D m_BodyType: 2 (Static), m_GravityScale: 1.
//       `Cave Exit`    TWO tiles, at x -8, y -3..-2 — a two-tile patch on the
//                      left-hand wall. UNTAGGED. The same three components as
//                      the floor, plus SceneSwitch.cs (guid 4790d855...,
//                      `scene: 1` = Overworld). The old page left this object
//                      out of the Hierarchy entirely and said the Grid had two
//                      children.
//       `No Collision` 85 tiles, bounding box 15 wide by 7 tall — MORE tiles
//                      than the floor has. TilemapRenderer only; NO collider
//                      of any kind, so a query can never hit it.
//     So the Grid has three children, not two, and the second solid one is the
//     object a tag-based check gets wrong (that argument belongs to 6.2/7.2).
//
//   Art: Assets/Artwork/Platformer/Sliced/CavesTileSet/ holds 1,829 .asset
//     Tile assets and CaveEntranceTileSet/ holds 250 — the old "hundreds of
//     them" understated both folders by an order of magnitude. Each sampled
//     .asset is a MonoBehaviour whose m_Script is Unity's built-in Tile
//     (fileID 13312), i.e. a Tile pointing at a sprite. `Caves.prefab` and
//     `CavesEntrance.prefab` really are tile palettes: the root carries a
//     `Palette Settings` component (Unity's built-in GridPalette, fileID
//     12395) and a `Layer1` child carrying Tilemap + TilemapRenderer.
//     There is NO Assets/Sprites folder and NO Assets/Tilemaps folder.
//
//   ProjectSettings/TagManager.asset: tags Coin, Enemy, Axe, Spikes, Ground,
//     GroundCheck — and NO `Ground` layer. (6.2 creates it.)
//
// PROTECTED BLOCKS — ids are POSITIONAL (src/lib/formify.ts), so nothing here
// is reordered, renumbered, re-counted or re-shaped. Baseline captured from the
// pre-edit file and held exactly:
